1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,024
Voice bots got faster every year.

2
00:00:02,975 --> 00:00:05,911
And patients got older at the same time.

3
00:00:05,911 --> 00:00:09,699
Nobody built a voice line for the people who need a pause.

4
00:00:09,699 --> 00:00:12,186
So we built the one that waits.

5
00:00:12,789 --> 00:00:16,876
This is a default voice bot, given an eighty-year-old caller.

6
00:00:16,826 --> 00:00:20,114
She pauses to think, and it cuts her off.

7
00:00:20,114 --> 00:00:25,289
She says Thursday, it hears Tuesday, and it stacks two questions at
once.

8
00:00:25,289 --> 00:00:29,289
Watch the counter: two interruptions in twelve seconds.

9
00:00:29,289 --> 00:00:33,176
This is exactly why older adults hang up on voice AI.

10
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:38,442
Now the same caller, the same long pauses, on the patient line.

11
00:00:38,391 --> 00:00:40,380
It simply waits.

12
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:42,704
One question at a time.

13
00:00:42,704 --> 00:00:49,366
It reads the whole visit back, day, date, time, doctor, and books only
on an explicit yes.

14
00:00:49,366 --> 00:00:57,067
Then it teaches every medication back, drug names boosted in the
keyterms, and issues a signed receipt her daughter can check.

15
00:00:57,067 --> 00:01:00,304
That booking just landed in a real database.

16
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:02,907
None of it is mocked.

17
00:01:02,856 --> 00:01:05,344
The visit lives in Postgres.

18
00:01:05,344 --> 00:01:09,394
Offer the same slot twice and the second call is rejected.

19
00:01:09,394 --> 00:01:15,132
Every action ends in an HMAC-signed receipt, and verification comes
back true.

20
00:01:15,132 --> 00:01:23,432
And the phone line is real too: Twilio logged an eight minute, eight
second call, straight to the agent over the public switched network.

21
00:01:24,049 --> 00:01:27,250
Here is a signed receipt from a completed call.

22
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:31,025
Verified, exactly as confirmed on the voice line.

23
00:01:31,025 --> 00:01:35,337
Now watch what happens when one character of the summary is changed.

24
00:01:35,337 --> 00:01:37,825
The signature fails instantly.

25
00:01:37,825 --> 00:01:42,849
That is the difference between a chatbot promise and a record your
family can trust.

26
00:01:43,459 --> 00:01:53,260
The demo runs on silverline voice dot vercel dot app, or just call
plus one eight oh four, three fifteen, nineteen eighty seven, and

27
00:01:53,209 --> 00:01:54,921
SilverLine.

28
00:01:54,921 --> 00:01:57,272
The voice line that waits.

